---
layout: base.njk
title: "The missing social layer of Clash Royale"
description: "Elixir is the missing social layer of Clash Royale: follow your friends and your clan, see how they play, and cheer them on. Free; everything inside needs an account."
permalink: /index.html
canonical: /
navActive: home
---
{#- The front door, signed out: sign in or join (the canvas's signed-out
    shell, Jamie's go 2026-11-12: "Approved: build the remaining canvas
    pieces (…, signed-out shell, …)"). The gate leads. Below it, Jamie's
    trim of 2026-11-12 ("trim the signed-out front page to the gate, three
    flat rows and a Drop line, moving the agent demo and counts to Docs and
    Status"): friends, your clan and highlights as three flat rows, Drop as
    one line, and the call to join. The agent exchange lives on Connect a
    client (/docs/connect-a-client), the record's counts on /data. Signed
    in, the same page offers Open Elixir.

    A row promises only what is live, and shows no number: a visitor here
    has no record and the page has nobody's to show. -#}
{%- set drop = familyBar.products | selectattr("game") | first %}
<div data-home>
<section class="home-gate" aria-labelledby="home-gate">
  <div class="home-gate__col">
    <span class="chip chip--ok" data-recording-now hidden><span class="chip__dot"></span>Recording now</span>
    <h1 class="home-title" id="home-gate">Keep up with your friends in Clash Royale</h1>
    <p class="home-lede">
      Elixir is the missing social layer of Clash Royale: follow your friends
      and your clan, see how they play, and cheer them on. Free to join.
    </p>
    <div class="home-gate__ways" data-session-face="out">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/signin?signup">Create an account</a>
      <a class="btn btn--lg" href="{{ familyBar.signIn.path }}">{{ familyBar.signIn.label }}</a>
    </div>
    <div class="home-gate__ways" data-session-face="in">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="{{ familyBar.products[0].path }}">Open Elixir</a>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote m-0" data-session-face="out">
      A shared highlight or battle link opens for anyone. Everything else is
      for members.
      <a href="{{ familyBar.sampleBattle.path }}">{{ familyBar.sampleBattle.label }}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="home-art">
    <img src="/assets/elixir-logo-288.webp" alt="Elixir: a purple elixir bottle wearing a gold crown" width="288" height="288" />
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-rows" aria-label="What Elixir does">
  <article class="home-row">
    <span class="home-row__icon">{% icon "heart", 20 %}</span>
    <h2 class="home-row__title">Follow your friends</h2>
    <p class="home-row__text">
      See every session your friends play, every new Arena and league they
      reach, and the battles they&rsquo;re proudest of, all in one feed. Tap
      to cheer them on. Every Monday, right after the reset, your digest
      catches you up (or every day, if you like).
    </p>
    <a class="home-row__link" href="/docs/follow-a-friend">Follow a friend ›</a>
  </article>

  <article class="home-row">
    <span class="home-row__icon">{% icon "users", 20 %}</span>
    <h2 class="home-row__title">Your clan&rsquo;s week</h2>
    <p class="home-row__text">
      Watch the River Race unfold and see where every clanmate stands.
      Leaders set the clan&rsquo;s rules once, then handle promotions,
      welcomes and goodbyes in one place. Looking for a clan? Find one that
      plays your way in the clan directory.
    </p>
    <span class="home-row__links">
      <a class="home-row__link" href="/docs/bring-your-clan">Bring your clan ›</a>
      <a class="home-row__link" href="/docs/clan-directory">The clan directory ›</a>
    </span>
  </article>

  <article class="home-row">
    <span class="home-row__icon">{% icon "message-square-quote", 20 %}</span>
    <h2 class="home-row__title">Show off your best battles</h2>
    <p class="home-row__text">
      Had a great battle? Verify your player, pick the battle and tell the
      story in your own words. Everyone who follows you sees it, and the link
      opens for anyone, no account needed.
    </p>
    <a class="home-row__link" href="/docs/battles#highlight-a-battle">Highlight a battle ›</a>
  </article>
</section>

{%- if drop %}
<p class="home-next">
  <span class="home-next__mark">{% icon drop.icon, 16 %}</span>
  <span>{{ drop.label }}, the game next door: learn your elixir costs cold, signed in with your Elixir account.
  <a href="{{ drop.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ drop.action }}, {{ drop.about }} (opens {{ drop.href | host }} in a new window)">{{ drop.action }} ›</a></span>
</p>
{%- endif %}

{#- The FORM LIVES IN THE APP (2026-09-10), on the sign-in card: signing
    in and asking to are one decision. This call posts nothing; signup and
    sign-in share one email verification door. -#}
<section class="home-join" id="request" data-session-face="out" aria-labelledby="home-request">
  <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
    <h2 class="home-join__title" id="home-request">Create your account</h2>
    <p class="footnote m-0">Free. Verify your email, add your player tag, and you&rsquo;re in.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signin?signup">Create your account</a>
</section>
</div>

<script src="{{ "/assets/home-status.js" | asset }}" defer></script>
